WEBVTT

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.670
Animali!

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.538
Bruti animali!

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.136
Animali!

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.171
No, Leonardo,
you are the animal!

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.309
A bird who cannot fly!

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.683
Better than a man
who cannot think!

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.687
The pigeon speaks!

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.518
Maestro!

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.252
Stupido!

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.526
Foolish Florentines!

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.737
A bird is
a mechanical instrument

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:42.173
that works according
to mathematical laws.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.972
An instrument that surely
I can recreate.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.979
How did it fail?

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.846
Maybe you underestimated
the wingspan.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.010
Had not the River Arno
taken us to its arms,

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.643
we would both have died.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.018
Jumping off the bridge
was a wise precaution.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.683
Against death, yes.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.718
Against humiliation... no.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:08.564
"The great bird will take flight
and bring glory to its nest"...

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.967
so I have bragged for months.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:16.306
Instead, we almost drown
with half of Florence watching.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.979
Finito!

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.138
No more.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.172
Catarina...

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.980
have you been to France?

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:28.315
Not recently.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.653
Ah. The king of France
is a great admirer of mine.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.989
"The divine Leonardo"
is all I hear

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.755
when I walk through his streets.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:39.287
And what music do I find
in the streets of Florence, eh?

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:43.564
The cooing of pigeons
and the babbling of fools.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.503
Catarina, we are leaving.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.169
You're giving up.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.008
Hmm?

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.104
Again.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.912
Your beautiful painting
of the Adoration...

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.409
the great bronze horse
in Milan...

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.217
the Battle of Anghiari...

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.315
unfinished, all of them.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.757
You were going to publish
your notebooks.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.760
You never did.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.354
You have given up...

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.297
abandoned
your most important works.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.357
Why?

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.133
There is a...

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.870
a tavern just outside Paris,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.607
Catarina, a charming bistro
where the wine is...

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.815
Terramotto.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:30.816
Janeway to the Bridge.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.215
We're under attack, Captain.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.742
I'm on my way.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.784
Earthquakes... and idiots.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.819
Florence be damned.

00:04:43.281 --> 00:04:44.805
Who are they and why
are they shooting at us?

00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:45.816
Unknown, Captain.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.976
They're not responding
to hails.

00:04:47.018 --> 00:04:47.985
Damage?

00:04:48.019 --> 00:04:48.986
None.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.079
I'm reading
a slight destabilization

00:04:51.122 --> 00:04:52.089
along the shield perimeter.

00:04:52.123 --> 00:04:53.920
Attempting to compensate.

00:05:03.401 --> 00:05:04.800
Uh, Torres to the Bridge.

00:05:04.836 --> 00:05:05.803
Go ahead.

00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:07.828
We just lost
the warp diagnostic assembly.

00:05:07.872 --> 00:05:08.930
What do you mean "lost"?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.200
It disappeared.

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.545
I'm picking up
dematerializations on Decks 4

00:05:22.587 --> 00:05:24.214
- through 12.
- Evasive maneuvers.

00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:27.520
They're matching
our course changes.

00:05:37.068 --> 00:05:39.832
It's definitely some kind
of transporter beam.

00:05:39.871 --> 00:05:41.668
Fire at will.

00:05:41.706 --> 00:05:42.968
I have the will,

00:05:43.074 --> 00:05:44.268
but not the means, Captain.

00:05:44.308 --> 00:05:45.832
Targeting control is down.

00:05:45.877 --> 00:05:46.901
Why?

00:05:46.944 --> 00:05:49.504
Captain, the main
computer processor is gone.

00:05:49.547 --> 00:05:52.311
We've lost weapons, navigation
and propulsion.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.341
Backup systems
are coming on line.

00:05:54.385 --> 00:05:55.818
Full phasers, manual targeting,

00:05:55.853 --> 00:05:58.048
keep firing
until you hit something.

00:06:02.093 --> 00:06:04.118
The other ships are retreating.

00:06:04.162 --> 00:06:05.129
Chakotay to all decks.

00:06:05.163 --> 00:06:07.028
Full damage reports.

00:06:07.065 --> 00:06:10.034
I feel like
we've just been mugged.

00:06:19.911 --> 00:06:22.436
They were employing
a high-energy transporter beam

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.074
designed to locate objects
of technological value

00:06:25.116 --> 00:06:26.481
and remove them.

00:06:26.517 --> 00:06:28.382
They removed a lot.

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:30.580
Five tricorders,
three phaser rifles,

00:06:30.621 --> 00:06:33.385
a couple of photon
torpedo casings,

00:06:33.424 --> 00:06:34.789
two antimatter injectors,

00:06:34.826 --> 00:06:36.589
a month's supply
of emergency rations.

00:06:36.627 --> 00:06:38.151
No great loss there.

00:06:38.196 --> 00:06:39.288
Excuse me.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.355
You're forgetting
the most important thing

00:06:41.399 --> 00:06:43.390
of all... my mobile emitter.

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:44.731
Without it,
I'm stuck in Sick Bay.

00:06:44.769 --> 00:06:45.736
I can't go anywhere.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.362
We'll do
the best we can, Doctor,

00:06:47.405 --> 00:06:50.670
but our top priority is
the main computer processor.

00:06:50.708 --> 00:06:52.642
B'Elanna, I want a defense
against another

00:06:52.677 --> 00:06:54.304
transporter attack.

00:06:54.345 --> 00:06:56.245
Harry, do everything you can
to track

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.770
- those ships.
- Yes, ma'am.

00:06:57.815 --> 00:06:58.839
Dismissed.

00:07:02.887 --> 00:07:05.447
Seven... hey...

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.924
If you're here to fraternize,
I do not have the time.

00:07:08.025 --> 00:07:10.084
Actually, the Captain
wanted me to locate

00:07:10.128 --> 00:07:11.493
the ships that attacked us.

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:12.860
I've pushed
the long-range sensors

00:07:12.897 --> 00:07:14.057
about as far as they'll go...

00:07:14.098 --> 00:07:15.861
And now you believe the
sensors can be extended

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.868
by using the deep space
imaging system.

00:07:17.902 --> 00:07:19.733
Well, yes.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.931
I've been working
on that exact procedure

00:07:22.006 --> 00:07:23.701
for the past two hours.

00:07:23.741 --> 00:07:25.709
Really?
Let's have a look.

00:07:25.743 --> 00:07:28.610
Do you doubt my ability
to finish the task?

00:07:28.646 --> 00:07:30.079
Lt...

00:07:30.114 --> 00:07:31.308
Look...

00:07:31.349 --> 00:07:33.943
I came here to work.

00:07:33.985 --> 00:07:37.921
Um... I realized you'd
already started the job...

00:07:37.955 --> 00:07:40.253
so I offered to help.

00:07:40.291 --> 00:07:41.280
That's all.

00:07:42.293 --> 00:07:43.817
I offered to help.

00:07:45.129 --> 00:07:46.323
An algorithmic feedback

00:07:46.364 --> 00:07:48.229
is interfering
with the resolution.

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:51.099
Decompile data banks
59 through 17

00:07:51.135 --> 00:07:52.568
and attempt to isolate it.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:56.871
Now...

00:07:58.009 --> 00:07:59.943
or you should leave.

00:07:59.977 --> 00:08:01.945
Okay.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.075
I'm a pretty easygoing person.

00:08:08.119 --> 00:08:09.814
I mean, it takes a lot to...

00:08:09.854 --> 00:08:11.549
ruffle my... feathers.

00:08:13.124 --> 00:08:15.649
But that's not true
of everybody.

00:08:15.693 --> 00:08:18.093
You've got to learn
how to phrase things

00:08:18.129 --> 00:08:20.962
a little more...
diplomatically.

00:08:24.835 --> 00:08:26.268
Or not.

00:08:29.907 --> 00:08:34.367
Captain's Log, Stardate 51386.4.

00:08:34.412 --> 00:08:37.142
With ship's systems
at nearly half capacity,

00:08:37.181 --> 00:08:41.413
it's taken us ten days
to track our stolen technology.

00:08:41.452 --> 00:08:42.942
I'm picking up
Starfleet signatures

00:08:42.987 --> 00:08:44.579
from two of the continents.

00:08:44.622 --> 00:08:46.852
Can you find the main
computer processor?

00:08:46.891 --> 00:08:51.021
It's on the northern continent
in what looks like a city...

00:08:52.096 --> 00:08:53.620
but there's a lot
of signal interference.

00:08:53.664 --> 00:08:55.291
I'll never be able
to localize it from here.

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.767
Captain, I've identified

00:08:57.802 --> 00:09:01.033
nearly 27 kinds of alien ships
in orbit of this planet.

00:09:01.072 --> 00:09:03.438
It appears to be an active
center of commerce.

00:09:03.474 --> 00:09:05.237
We should be able to place
an undercover away team

00:09:05.276 --> 00:09:07.642
on either continent
without attracting attention.

00:09:07.678 --> 00:09:08.906
That's good enough for now.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.073
Tuvok, you and I
are going after the processor.

00:09:11.115 --> 00:09:12.275
Tom, Neelix, I want you

00:09:12.316 --> 00:09:14.045
on the other continent,
find out what you can.

00:09:14.085 --> 00:09:17.521
At the very least, try to get
our emergency rations back.

00:09:17.555 --> 00:09:18.954
Chakotay, you have the Bridge.

00:09:40.911 --> 00:09:42.811
It never fails to impress me.

00:09:42.846 --> 00:09:44.211
No matter how vast
the differences

00:09:44.247 --> 00:09:46.511
may be between cultures,
people always have something

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:49.383
that somebody else wants
and trade is born.

00:09:49.419 --> 00:09:51.284
Or more to the point, theft.

00:09:51.321 --> 00:09:52.481
What have you got?

00:09:52.522 --> 00:09:54.956
The materials in
the construction of this city,

00:09:54.992 --> 00:09:56.482
and the technology in use

00:09:56.526 --> 00:09:58.357
appear to have originated
from numerous sources.

00:09:58.395 --> 00:09:59.794
No doubt stolen.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.491
The myriad signatures
have resulted

00:10:01.531 --> 00:10:02.930
in high interference levels.

00:10:02.966 --> 00:10:05.764
I am unable to...
A moment.

00:10:05.802 --> 00:10:07.736
I am picking up
a Starfleet signature.

00:10:07.771 --> 00:10:08.863
The computer processor?

00:10:08.905 --> 00:10:09.872
I don't believe so.

00:10:09.906 --> 00:10:11.874
The signal magnitude
is too low.

00:10:11.908 --> 00:10:14.638
The signature is...

00:10:14.678 --> 00:10:15.940
approaching.

00:10:15.979 --> 00:10:17.241
Catarina!

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.611
Che maraviglia!

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:19.479
Out of my way!

00:10:19.516 --> 00:10:21.074
Out of my way!
Scusa.

00:10:21.118 --> 00:10:22.085
Perdono.

00:10:22.119 --> 00:10:23.313
Catarina!

00:10:24.755 --> 00:10:25.779
Welcome!

00:10:25.822 --> 00:10:28.484
Welcome to America!

00:10:40.971 --> 00:10:42.302
Tell me, Catarina,

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:43.738
what do you think
of the New World?

00:10:43.774 --> 00:10:45.241
How did you get here?

00:10:45.275 --> 00:10:47.835
A question I have
asked myself many times.

00:10:47.878 --> 00:10:50.108
One moment, I was packing
for my journey to France,

00:10:50.147 --> 00:10:52.638
the next, I was in this land
of marvels.

00:10:52.683 --> 00:10:55.914
Possibly, upon leaving
my workshop,

00:10:55.952 --> 00:10:58.352
I was accosted
by Spanish sailors...

00:10:58.388 --> 00:11:01.050
rendered unconscious,
delivered to a galleon

00:11:01.091 --> 00:11:03.719
in the port
of Genoa and carried

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.957
like a sack of grain
across the vast Atlantic.

00:11:07.064 --> 00:11:08.554
Curious ears.

00:11:08.598 --> 00:11:11.931
My traveling companion,
Tuvok.

00:11:11.968 --> 00:11:15.404
Oh, what the old
philosophers say is true...

00:11:15.439 --> 00:11:17.930
"monstrous and wonderful
are the peoples

00:11:17.974 --> 00:11:19.908
of undiscovered lands."

00:11:19.943 --> 00:11:21.774
But tell me, Catarina...

00:11:21.812 --> 00:11:24.110
how did you come
to the Americas?

00:11:24.147 --> 00:11:26.547
Oh, it's a long story.

00:11:26.583 --> 00:11:30.075
A Portuguese ship,
some Turkish pirates...

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.087
a couple of hurricanes...

00:11:31.121 --> 00:11:32.679
I'll tell you all about
it some other time.

00:11:32.723 --> 00:11:33.917
Excuse me.

00:11:33.957 --> 00:11:36.187
There is the man that I
have been looking for.

00:11:36.226 --> 00:11:38.091
He has an apparatus
that I need

00:11:38.128 --> 00:11:39.891
for my next invention.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:41.795
My patron is
a demanding taskmaster.

00:11:41.832 --> 00:11:43.163
Your patron?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.101
The prince of this city.

00:11:46.136 --> 00:11:49.037
Buon giorno, signori.

00:11:50.807 --> 00:11:53.241
The da Vinci character
is interpreting this world

00:11:53.276 --> 00:11:55.403
through the limited capacity
of his holodeck program.

00:11:55.445 --> 00:11:57.936
He sees everything
in 16th century terms.

00:11:57.981 --> 00:11:59.471
But what is he doing here?

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.415
I was running
the da Vinci simulation

00:12:02.452 --> 00:12:03.817
when we were attacked.

00:12:03.854 --> 00:12:07.950
His program must have been
active in the computer's memory

00:12:08.024 --> 00:12:10.515
when the processor
was beamed off the ship.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.188
And then downloaded into
the Doctor's mobile emitter.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.595
But by whom?

00:12:14.631 --> 00:12:16.155
His patron?

00:12:16.199 --> 00:12:17.496
The prince?

00:12:22.372 --> 00:12:24.806
Marvelous, no?

00:12:24.841 --> 00:12:27.309
A plasma injector conduit.

00:12:27.344 --> 00:12:28.641
Starfleet issue.

00:12:28.678 --> 00:12:30.077
Call it what you will.

00:12:30.113 --> 00:12:31.580
With this machine, I can make

00:12:31.615 --> 00:12:34.106
mercury flow
in three directions at once.

00:12:34.151 --> 00:12:35.982
You must see my new workshop.

00:12:36.052 --> 00:12:37.576
The prince has been
very supportive.

00:12:37.621 --> 00:12:38.610
Andiamo.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.384
Let's go.

00:12:49.666 --> 00:12:51.600
So, Catarina...

00:12:51.635 --> 00:12:53.500
what do you think of this place?

00:12:55.372 --> 00:12:56.771
My workshop in Florence

00:12:56.807 --> 00:12:59.332
was but a cave of ignorance
in comparison.

00:12:59.376 --> 00:13:03.176
Your new patron
gave you all this?

00:13:03.213 --> 00:13:05.579
He is the perfect prince.

00:13:05.615 --> 00:13:08.584
Intelligent...
but not overly so.

00:13:08.618 --> 00:13:11.052
In awe of my talent,
but not threatened by it.

00:13:11.087 --> 00:13:14.215
And above all,
and most importantly,

00:13:14.257 --> 00:13:17.192
his purse is inexhaustible.

00:13:17.227 --> 00:13:21.163
And in return
for all this support?

00:13:21.198 --> 00:13:22.790
I give him my ideas.

00:13:29.005 --> 00:13:31.132
I have even resurrected
my great bird,

00:13:31.174 --> 00:13:33.438
like the phoenix of legend.

00:13:33.476 --> 00:13:35.967
They have materials here,
Catarina,

00:13:36.012 --> 00:13:38.105
that are so strong and so light

00:13:38.148 --> 00:13:41.777
that surely my prototype
will ascend to the heavens.

00:13:47.557 --> 00:13:49.320
Be careful!

00:13:49.359 --> 00:13:51.725
They have found a way

00:13:51.761 --> 00:13:54.525
to harness the energy
of a thunderstorm

00:13:54.564 --> 00:13:56.657
and to expel it
with great force.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.362
A pistole that shoots
not a lead ball

00:13:59.402 --> 00:14:01.893
but a bolt of lightning.

00:14:08.612 --> 00:14:11.172
Well, I'd like to meet
this patron of yours.

00:14:11.214 --> 00:14:13.876
And so you shall
this very evening.

00:14:13.917 --> 00:14:15.316
But I caution you...

00:14:15.352 --> 00:14:18.480
he is as ruthless as a Borgia.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.354
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 51392.7.

00:14:28.398 --> 00:14:30.832
Though we've yet to hear
from the Captain and Tuvok,

00:14:30.867 --> 00:14:33.062
Paris and Neelix have returned
from their mission

00:14:33.103 --> 00:14:36.129
to the southern continent
with some disturbing evidence.

00:14:36.172 --> 00:14:37.901
Who sold you these things?

00:14:37.941 --> 00:14:40.171
I didn't come here
to be interrogated.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:42.440
You told me you had
a warp coil to trade.

00:14:42.479 --> 00:14:45.448
I said you could
talk with Commander Chakotay.

00:14:45.482 --> 00:14:48.246
I didn't say he'd necessarily
do business with you.

00:14:48.285 --> 00:14:49.616
Well, this is
a waste of my time.

00:14:49.653 --> 00:14:51.780
I agree.

00:14:51.821 --> 00:14:52.947
There's the door.

00:14:52.989 --> 00:14:53.751
What?!

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.621
Good-bye.
Make sure he doesn't

00:14:55.659 --> 00:14:56.683
get lost on the way out.

00:14:56.726 --> 00:14:58.125
No, wait, wait.

00:14:58.161 --> 00:15:00.186
His name is Tau.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:02.721
He controls the Seventh Province
in the North.

00:15:02.766 --> 00:15:03.926
He sells weapons and technology.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:04.932
Yes.

00:15:05.001 --> 00:15:07.060
Which he confiscates
from passing ships.

00:15:07.103 --> 00:15:09.128
Yes, using
his translocator device.

00:15:09.172 --> 00:15:10.764
Which he also stole.

00:15:10.807 --> 00:15:12.502
It's made him a rich man.

00:15:12.542 --> 00:15:15.067
There are a few items
I'd like to get back.

00:15:15.111 --> 00:15:16.635
Where can I find him?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.204
I deal with a go-between.

00:15:18.248 --> 00:15:21.479
I've answered enough
of your questions.

00:15:21.518 --> 00:15:23.145
Let's talk about that warp coil.

00:15:23.186 --> 00:15:24.153
I'm looking for something...

00:15:24.187 --> 00:15:25.779
You can keep what you've got.

00:15:25.822 --> 00:15:27.915
We'll call it even.

00:15:32.329 --> 00:15:34.229
This was a waste of my time.

00:15:34.264 --> 00:15:35.561
Not really.

00:15:35.598 --> 00:15:38.465
These colors look good on you.

00:15:45.008 --> 00:15:48.307
Torpedoes, plasma grenades...

00:15:48.345 --> 00:15:49.369
particle beam rifles...

00:15:49.412 --> 00:15:50.936
I can even get
a ceremonial spear

00:15:50.981 --> 00:15:52.380
if you're interested.

00:15:52.415 --> 00:15:54.315
I am not interested.

00:15:56.219 --> 00:15:58.915
My point is, no matter
what the weaponry,

00:15:58.955 --> 00:16:00.718
if you desire it,

00:16:00.757 --> 00:16:02.486
chances are I have it.

00:16:02.525 --> 00:16:04.652
Or I can get it.

00:16:11.067 --> 00:16:14.195
Your prices are said
to be unreasonable.

00:16:15.171 --> 00:16:17.571
"Unreasonable" is
such a strong term.

00:16:17.607 --> 00:16:18.733
But if I can't sell to you,

00:16:18.775 --> 00:16:20.140
I'll sell to one
of the other colonies

00:16:20.176 --> 00:16:21.336
in your system.

00:16:21.378 --> 00:16:23.676
A violent sort,
your neighbors, aren't they?

00:16:23.713 --> 00:16:25.772
I'd hate to make
your life difficult

00:16:25.815 --> 00:16:27.612
by offering my weapons to them.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.709
But if you don't
give me a choice...

00:16:32.155 --> 00:16:34.123
There can be no doubt

00:16:34.157 --> 00:16:36.387
our computer processor
is not in the city.

00:16:36.426 --> 00:16:38.621
Well, that certainly
makes things

00:16:38.661 --> 00:16:40.253
a little more difficult.

00:16:40.296 --> 00:16:43.356
Leonardo's new patron.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:44.731
He's quite the businessman.

00:16:44.768 --> 00:16:47.965
We may have no choice
but to do business with him.

00:16:48.071 --> 00:16:49.436
Catarina!

00:16:49.472 --> 00:16:52.168
Here are some friends
I want you to meet.

00:16:52.208 --> 00:16:54.506
Try to keep
our hologram occupied.

00:16:54.544 --> 00:16:55.909
But, Captain...

00:16:55.945 --> 00:16:57.469
Well, make small talk.

00:16:57.514 --> 00:16:59.505
Vulcans do not make small talk.

00:16:59.549 --> 00:17:01.016
Improvise.

00:17:03.219 --> 00:17:04.379
Thank you.

00:17:04.421 --> 00:17:05.752
That is very considerate.

00:17:05.789 --> 00:17:06.756
Catarina, wait a minute!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.156
Mr. Da Vinci, how have you been?

00:17:09.192 --> 00:17:10.921
Benissimo.
Now if you will pardon me.

00:17:10.994 --> 00:17:12.484
I wish to speak with you.

00:17:12.529 --> 00:17:13.587
What about?

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.927
About you.

00:17:14.998 --> 00:17:17.626
You are most intriguing.

00:17:17.667 --> 00:17:19.294
Ah, grazie.

00:17:19.335 --> 00:17:22.168
And you, Signore Tuvok,
are equally provocative.

00:17:22.205 --> 00:17:23.797
Where, exactly, are you from?

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:25.637
Scandinavia.

00:17:29.112 --> 00:17:33.572
So... what do
the Scandinavians think

00:17:33.616 --> 00:17:34.844
of this New World?

00:17:34.884 --> 00:17:37.751
It is... fascinating.

00:17:37.787 --> 00:17:39.687
And you are
obviously enjoying it.

00:17:39.722 --> 00:17:41.917
Beyond words.

00:17:41.958 --> 00:17:43.357
Yes.

00:17:43.393 --> 00:17:45.953
Italy is already
a fading memory.

00:17:45.995 --> 00:17:48.793
This city is full
of mechanical marvels,

00:17:48.832 --> 00:17:50.925
the countryside
alive with creatures

00:17:50.967 --> 00:17:54.403
strange and wonderful.

00:17:54.437 --> 00:17:56.064
I'm curious.

00:17:56.106 --> 00:17:58.301
How have you spent
your time here?

00:17:58.341 --> 00:18:03.677
I work... on my
inventions and my art,

00:18:03.713 --> 00:18:07.205
and I accompany the prince

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.986
when he goes to visit
his great fortresses.

00:18:10.119 --> 00:18:12.417
Well, this fascinating
conversation...

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.554
has left me as dry as Vulcan.

00:18:16.592 --> 00:18:18.150
Vulcan?

00:18:18.194 --> 00:18:19.923
An island off Sicily.
Have you been there?

00:18:20.029 --> 00:18:21.894
No.

00:18:21.931 --> 00:18:23.262
Pity.

00:18:33.776 --> 00:18:35.641
We'll talk later.

00:18:35.678 --> 00:18:37.509
Good evening.

00:18:37.546 --> 00:18:39.446
And to you.

00:18:39.482 --> 00:18:42.042
Enjoying yourself?

00:18:42.084 --> 00:18:43.051
Not yet.

00:18:43.085 --> 00:18:44.109
No?

00:18:44.153 --> 00:18:45.950
How can I change that?

00:18:46.022 --> 00:18:47.546
By having exactly what I want

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.490
and selling it to me
at a low price.

00:18:51.127 --> 00:18:53.118
The former's quite likely,
but as for the latter,

00:18:53.162 --> 00:18:56.063
I don't sell
inexpensive merchandise.

00:18:56.098 --> 00:18:58.328
I have a client
who runs a colony

00:18:58.367 --> 00:19:00.301
about 20 parsecs from here.

00:19:00.336 --> 00:19:02.361
His computer is outmoded,

00:19:02.405 --> 00:19:05.306
so I'm... looking
for a replacement.

00:19:05.341 --> 00:19:10.210
A computer that could coordinate
the systems of an entire colony.

00:19:10.246 --> 00:19:12.271
That's no small order.

00:19:12.314 --> 00:19:13.747
But I think
I might have something

00:19:13.783 --> 00:19:14.807
that will interest you.

00:19:24.126 --> 00:19:26.754
Hello, Computer,
and how are you today?

00:19:26.796 --> 00:19:30.493
All systems are functioning
within normal parameters.

00:19:30.533 --> 00:19:34.663
Verbal interface.
Impressive.

00:19:34.703 --> 00:19:39.231
Computer, tell us
your technical specifications.

00:19:39.275 --> 00:19:42.802
Simultaneous access
to 47 million data channels,

00:19:42.845 --> 00:19:44.813
transluminal processing

00:19:44.847 --> 00:19:47.816
at 575 trillion calculations
per nanosecond.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.215
Interested?

00:19:49.251 --> 00:19:52.084
Operational temperature margins
from ten degrees kelvin

00:19:52.121 --> 00:19:54.385
to 1,790 degrees kelvin.

00:19:54.423 --> 00:19:56.186
I could sell it to you,

00:19:56.225 --> 00:20:00.059
but I could hardly let it go
for anything less than...

00:20:00.096 --> 00:20:01.563
a warship.

00:20:03.899 --> 00:20:06.732
Or we could find something else
in your price range.

00:20:19.982 --> 00:20:21.711
We should be looking
for a stronghold

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.978
or storage facility...

00:20:23.052 --> 00:20:25.987
anyplace Tau might keep
the stolen technology.

00:20:26.055 --> 00:20:27.989
There are
several possibilities,

00:20:28.057 --> 00:20:30.992
all within a ten-kilometer
radius of the city.

00:20:31.026 --> 00:20:35.895
I must admit, your Mr. Da Vinci
is an astute observer of nature.

00:20:35.931 --> 00:20:37.728
These maps
couldn't be improved upon

00:20:37.766 --> 00:20:39.529
by Voyager's
topographical computer.

00:20:39.568 --> 00:20:42.935
He was a Renaissance man, Tuvok.

00:20:42.972 --> 00:20:47.705
Interpreted, reinterpreted,
deconstructed, fantasized about

00:20:47.743 --> 00:20:49.438
all through history.

00:20:49.478 --> 00:20:51.571
Vasari thought he was an angel.

00:20:51.614 --> 00:20:54.014
Freud thought he had
a problem with his mother.

00:20:54.116 --> 00:20:56.016
James T. Kirk
claimed he met him,

00:20:56.085 --> 00:20:58.019
although the evidence
is less than conclusive.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:59.519
Buon giorno, amici.

00:20:59.555 --> 00:21:01.318
Good morning, Maestro.

00:21:01.357 --> 00:21:02.324
Did you sleep well?

00:21:02.358 --> 00:21:03.723
Too well, I'm afraid.

00:21:03.759 --> 00:21:06.922
My apologies, Catarina.

00:21:06.962 --> 00:21:08.259
The morning is half gone.

00:21:08.297 --> 00:21:10.128
Nevertheless, the images

00:21:10.166 --> 00:21:13.226
that come before the eyes
upon awakening

00:21:13.269 --> 00:21:15.100
can be inspiring.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.275
Indeed.

00:21:23.312 --> 00:21:26.281
Catarina, where did I leave
my silver-tip pen?

00:21:26.315 --> 00:21:27.748
I could swear
it was here on...

00:21:27.783 --> 00:21:30.775
Captain, we should
return to Voyager.

00:21:30.819 --> 00:21:33.947
With my tricorder readings
and Leonardo's maps,

00:21:33.989 --> 00:21:36.287
we can use the ship's sensors
to triangulate

00:21:36.325 --> 00:21:38.225
the exact location
of our processor.

00:21:40.563 --> 00:21:42.758
We'll work on two fronts.

00:21:42.798 --> 00:21:43.992
You go back to the ship.

00:21:44.033 --> 00:21:45.796
I'll stay on the surface and
keep working with Leonardo.

00:21:45.834 --> 00:21:46.926
He has access to Tau

00:21:46.969 --> 00:21:48.459
and he knows the territory.

00:21:48.504 --> 00:21:49.766
Inadvisable.

00:21:49.805 --> 00:21:52.535
Charming as your childhood hero
may be,

00:21:52.575 --> 00:21:55.271
the program was not designed
for use outside the holodeck.

00:21:55.311 --> 00:21:57.836
This is Leonardo da Vinci
we're talking about.

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.280
Simulation or not,
he's one of the greatest

00:22:00.316 --> 00:22:02.250
creative minds
in Earth's history.

00:22:02.284 --> 00:22:04.946
The program reproduces
the entire range

00:22:04.987 --> 00:22:07.854
of da Vinci's behavior...
his genius

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:10.120
and his notorious
unreliability.

00:22:10.159 --> 00:22:12.286
We have an opportunity here...

00:22:14.597 --> 00:22:16.929
and I want
to take advantage of it.

00:22:23.606 --> 00:22:24.937
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:22:24.974 --> 00:22:26.407
One to beam up.

00:22:34.683 --> 00:22:36.173
...table.

00:22:36.218 --> 00:22:37.378
Where did he go?

00:22:37.419 --> 00:22:39.080
Back to the ship.

00:22:39.121 --> 00:22:40.486
The ship?!

00:22:40.522 --> 00:22:44.083
You mean, the Portuguese
are still in the harbor?

00:22:44.126 --> 00:22:49.120
Well... not exactly...
but they're nearby.

00:22:49.164 --> 00:22:51.325
Ah.

00:22:51.367 --> 00:22:54.461
Mad sea dogs, the Portuguese.

00:23:02.411 --> 00:23:05.437
So, what's new?

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:06.879
New?

00:23:06.915 --> 00:23:08.576
What's been happening
on the ship?

00:23:08.617 --> 00:23:10.084
Nothing of consequence.

00:23:10.118 --> 00:23:11.085
The Captain and Tuvok

00:23:11.119 --> 00:23:12.848
are still searching
for the processor.

00:23:12.888 --> 00:23:14.947
What's the mood?

00:23:15.056 --> 00:23:17.115
If you're referring
to the crew morale,

00:23:17.159 --> 00:23:19.787
they seem focused
on their mission.

00:23:19.828 --> 00:23:23.195
Hmm. I heard there was
something of a fuss

00:23:23.231 --> 00:23:24.391
in the Mess Hall last night.

00:23:24.433 --> 00:23:25.957
A trivial misunderstanding.

00:23:26.001 --> 00:23:27.366
Oh?

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:31.134
Well, you seem
in excellent health.

00:23:31.173 --> 00:23:32.868
Most of your implants
are stable,

00:23:32.908 --> 00:23:36.139
but your optical interface
is misaligned again.

00:23:36.178 --> 00:23:40.137
I told you to come in
for maintenance once a week.

00:23:40.182 --> 00:23:45.279
So... what happened
in the Mess Hall?

00:23:47.923 --> 00:23:49.914
Lieutenant Torres
and I were working

00:23:49.958 --> 00:23:51.425
on some astrometric data.

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:52.722
There was a disagreement.

00:23:52.761 --> 00:23:55.423
I understand things got
a little... heated.

00:23:55.464 --> 00:23:57.796
Lieutenant Torres
became emotional.

00:23:57.833 --> 00:23:59.698
She chose to display hostility

00:23:59.734 --> 00:24:01.531
rather than to counter
my argument.

00:24:01.570 --> 00:24:03.333
What did she say exactly?

00:24:03.371 --> 00:24:04.395
It is irrelevant.

00:24:04.439 --> 00:24:06.498
Suffice it to say,
I was correct.

00:24:06.541 --> 00:24:07.530
She was not.

00:24:07.576 --> 00:24:10.670
Details, Seven,
I want specifics.

00:24:10.712 --> 00:24:13.545
I see no reason to discuss
these trivialities.

00:24:13.582 --> 00:24:15.948
Without my mobile emitter,
I am a prisoner in here.

00:24:15.984 --> 00:24:17.781
I need to know
what is going on

00:24:17.819 --> 00:24:19.912
beyond these walls,
trivial or not.

00:24:22.657 --> 00:24:24.921
Torres referred to me
as an automaton.

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:26.222
She also employed

00:24:26.261 --> 00:24:29.059
a series of profane
Klingon insults.

00:24:29.097 --> 00:24:31.190
Shall I translate them for you?

00:24:31.233 --> 00:24:32.461
By all means.
I very much...

00:24:32.501 --> 00:24:33.968
Tuvok to Seven of Nine.

00:24:34.069 --> 00:24:36.367
Report to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:24:36.404 --> 00:24:38.872
You may go.

00:24:38.907 --> 00:24:40.169
I'll be right there, Commander.

00:24:40.208 --> 00:24:41.937
Come back whenever you feel
like talking.

00:24:41.977 --> 00:24:45.936
I'll be right here...
all by myself.

00:24:50.218 --> 00:24:51.879
I'm entering Leonardo's maps

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:54.787
and my tricorder data
into the imaging system.

00:24:54.823 --> 00:24:55.983
I will create
a search pattern

00:24:56.057 --> 00:24:57.718
for our missing processor.

00:24:57.759 --> 00:24:59.386
Da Vinci has
accurately rendered

00:24:59.427 --> 00:25:00.792
the topographical detail.

00:25:00.829 --> 00:25:03.730
However, his coordinate
axes are pre-Cartesian.

00:25:03.765 --> 00:25:05.289
You will have to convert them.

00:25:05.333 --> 00:25:06.527
Understood.

00:25:08.203 --> 00:25:09.397
It is puzzling that even

00:25:09.437 --> 00:25:11.632
a Vulcan would refer
to a holographic character

00:25:11.673 --> 00:25:13.766
by name, as if it were alive.

00:25:13.808 --> 00:25:17.574
It seems somehow... illogical.

00:25:20.916 --> 00:25:22.907
Localizing grid.

00:25:23.952 --> 00:25:25.920
Altitude:
20 kilometers.

00:25:25.954 --> 00:25:27.387
One of these
storage facilities

00:25:27.422 --> 00:25:29.083
undoubtedly contains
the processor.

00:25:29.124 --> 00:25:32.252
Increase sensor resolution
to maximum and scan the area.

00:25:35.463 --> 00:25:36.657
There.

00:25:36.698 --> 00:25:39.326
Our computer processor
is inside this structure.

00:25:39.367 --> 00:25:41.426
Unfortunately, the building

00:25:41.469 --> 00:25:43.437
is surrounded
by a dispersion field.

00:25:43.471 --> 00:25:45.166
Transport will be impossible.

00:25:45.206 --> 00:25:47.367
If the Captain can get
inside the facility

00:25:47.409 --> 00:25:50.640
and reach the processor itself,
she may be able to assist us.

00:25:50.679 --> 00:25:54.775
If she were to initiate
a power surge in the processor,

00:25:54.816 --> 00:25:57.944
it might produce a signal strong
enough for us to lock onto.

00:25:57.986 --> 00:25:59.977
That is what I was referring to.

00:26:00.088 --> 00:26:02.113
I will inform the Captain.

00:26:12.367 --> 00:26:14.927
It's not too far,
across open country.

00:26:15.003 --> 00:26:18.837
Leonardo says he's been there,
and he can help me get inside.

00:26:18.873 --> 00:26:20.067
Understood.

00:26:20.108 --> 00:26:21.632
Stand by for my signal.

00:26:21.676 --> 00:26:23.166
If I can find the processor,

00:26:23.211 --> 00:26:25.611
be prepared
to beam it back to Voyager.

00:26:25.647 --> 00:26:26.614
Aye, Captain.

00:26:26.648 --> 00:26:27.672
Tuvok out.

00:26:28.883 --> 00:26:31.113
So it's Captain?

00:26:31.152 --> 00:26:35.088
I see you and my hologram
are old friends.

00:26:54.876 --> 00:26:56.935
My engineers have
developed a defense

00:26:56.978 --> 00:26:58.639
against your transporter,

00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:01.513
so I suggest you return
what you took from us

00:27:01.549 --> 00:27:02.846
and let me go.

00:27:02.884 --> 00:27:04.408
Or what?

00:27:04.452 --> 00:27:06.113
You're in no position
to bargain.

00:27:06.154 --> 00:27:08.019
The only ones who will
bargain will be your crew

00:27:08.056 --> 00:27:09.216
and it'll cost them

00:27:09.257 --> 00:27:12.055
a great deal to get
their Captain back.

00:27:12.093 --> 00:27:13.958
I wonder what you're
worth to them...

00:27:17.465 --> 00:27:18.489
He'll be fine.

00:27:18.533 --> 00:27:19.864
Let's move.

00:27:19.901 --> 00:27:20.925
I'm not going.

00:27:21.036 --> 00:27:22.060
You said you'd help me.

00:27:22.103 --> 00:27:23.695
I have already gone too far.

00:27:23.738 --> 00:27:26.070
He was threatening you,
I had no alternative.

00:27:26.107 --> 00:27:28.268
But I must be here
when he recovers his senses.

00:27:28.309 --> 00:27:29.435
I will try to explain.

00:27:29.477 --> 00:27:31.536
Maybe, if I am lucky,
he will not have me executed.

00:27:31.579 --> 00:27:32.546
We are leaving.

00:27:32.580 --> 00:27:33.706
Your time here is over.

00:27:33.748 --> 00:27:35.648
I will not leave this New World!

00:27:35.684 --> 00:27:37.413
Your New World is a prison.

00:27:37.452 --> 00:27:38.646
You are under his control.

00:27:38.687 --> 00:27:39.813
When are we not in prison?

00:27:39.854 --> 00:27:40.946
Hmm?

00:27:40.989 --> 00:27:43.150
When are our lives free
from the influence

00:27:43.191 --> 00:27:45.159
of those who have
more power than us?

00:27:46.861 --> 00:27:51.855
If this New World is a cage,
than it is a cage of gold,

00:27:51.900 --> 00:27:53.390
of marvels...

00:27:53.435 --> 00:27:55.426
of opportunities.

00:27:55.470 --> 00:27:59.907
If this prince is violent,
violence can be tempered.

00:27:59.941 --> 00:28:01.909
But you can't stay
here forever, Leonardo.

00:28:01.976 --> 00:28:03.637
Europe is your home.

00:28:03.678 --> 00:28:05.908
Europe is despicable.

00:28:06.014 --> 00:28:09.643
Here I am free to do
what I wish,

00:28:09.684 --> 00:28:12.448
free from judgment,
free to fail...

00:28:12.487 --> 00:28:15.251
without a sense
of shame, without...

00:28:15.290 --> 00:28:17.383
without the taunts
of the ignorant.

00:28:17.425 --> 00:28:20.292
Leonardo, whether you want
to admit it or not,

00:28:20.328 --> 00:28:22.660
they do need you back home.

00:28:22.697 --> 00:28:25.757
In Florence, Milan, Avignon...

00:28:25.800 --> 00:28:29.258
they need your genius,
they need your heart

00:28:29.304 --> 00:28:31.772
and right now, I need you, too.

00:28:31.806 --> 00:28:32.898
So come on.

00:28:36.644 --> 00:28:38.874
I will not go...

00:28:38.913 --> 00:28:42.815
for Florence or Milan
or Avignon...

00:28:44.853 --> 00:28:46.514
but for you, Catarina...

00:28:49.991 --> 00:28:51.856
for you, I will go.

00:29:01.268 --> 00:29:03.634
I've lost the Captain's
combadge signature.

00:29:03.670 --> 00:29:05.865
Scan for the holo-emitter.

00:29:08.675 --> 00:29:11.644
It's 4.7 kilometers
outside the city.

00:29:11.678 --> 00:29:13.168
So Leonardo's on the move.

00:29:13.213 --> 00:29:14.680
Is the Captain with him?

00:29:14.715 --> 00:29:16.808
Her combadge may have
malfunctioned.

00:29:16.850 --> 00:29:18.078
Or she might have been
discovered.

00:29:18.118 --> 00:29:20.086
Should I beam da Vinci
back to the ship?

00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:21.246
If the Captain is with him

00:29:21.288 --> 00:29:23.051
and attempting to recover
the processor,

00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:24.387
she may need his assistance.

00:29:26.093 --> 00:29:27.492
Keep a lock
on the mobile emitter

00:29:27.528 --> 00:29:28.517
and stand by.

00:29:28.562 --> 00:29:29.551
Aye, sir.

00:29:34.067 --> 00:29:35.091
Where's the entrance?

00:29:35.135 --> 00:29:36.159
I can't recall.

00:29:36.203 --> 00:29:37.170
Why not?

00:29:37.204 --> 00:29:38.671
These fortresses...

00:29:38.705 --> 00:29:40.172
I've been to half a dozen
of them.

00:29:40.207 --> 00:29:41.936
All are similar,
but each is different.

00:30:08.402 --> 00:30:11.200
Catarina,
observe the construction...

00:30:11.238 --> 00:30:14.230
like the veins and arteries
of a great animal.

00:30:14.274 --> 00:30:16.469
Now, this is the way to build...
using nature as your guide.

00:30:16.510 --> 00:30:17.477
No more lessons.

00:30:17.511 --> 00:30:18.478
I need to get into

00:30:18.512 --> 00:30:20.241
this building and I need
to get into it now.

00:30:20.280 --> 00:30:21.611
That is not the way

00:30:21.648 --> 00:30:24.048
an apprentice should address
her master.

00:30:27.054 --> 00:30:30.490
Maestro, your prince is
going to come after us.

00:30:30.524 --> 00:30:32.424
The only escape is inside.

00:30:32.459 --> 00:30:33.517
Escape?

00:30:33.560 --> 00:30:35.460
We will be trapped inside.

00:30:35.496 --> 00:30:38.124
No. There is a wondrous
invention inside this building.

00:30:38.165 --> 00:30:40.292
It's called
a computer processor.

00:30:40.334 --> 00:30:42.564
We can use to send
a beacon to...

00:30:42.603 --> 00:30:44.366
to the Portuguese ship.

00:30:44.404 --> 00:30:46.338
And they'll come
and rescue us.

00:30:46.373 --> 00:30:47.863
Computer?

00:30:47.908 --> 00:30:50.172
This invention,
how does it work?

00:30:50.210 --> 00:30:51.973
Well, it's complicated...

00:30:52.012 --> 00:30:53.104
but trust me when I say

00:30:53.146 --> 00:30:55.137
it can send messages
over great distances.

00:30:55.182 --> 00:30:57.446
All we have to do is find it
and we will be rescued.

00:30:57.484 --> 00:31:00.317
But the question is:
How do we get inside?

00:31:05.158 --> 00:31:07.592
Shadow and sunlight.

00:31:09.530 --> 00:31:11.395
Shadow and sunlight.

00:31:15.135 --> 00:31:17.126
The prince,
like any other thief,

00:31:17.170 --> 00:31:20.196
will fear theft above all else.

00:31:20.240 --> 00:31:23.141
So this stronghold will
have but one entryway...

00:31:23.176 --> 00:31:26.509
on the side facing
away from the sun.

00:31:26.547 --> 00:31:27.514
So the bright light

00:31:27.548 --> 00:31:29.448
would be in the eyes of
anyone who might attack.

00:31:29.483 --> 00:31:31.644
Esatto.

00:31:38.191 --> 00:31:39.988
Hmm...

00:31:40.027 --> 00:31:42.723
I'm no longer reading
the mobile emitter.

00:31:43.664 --> 00:31:45.529
They've gone inside
the structure.

00:31:45.566 --> 00:31:47.727
Commander,
they are being pursued.

00:31:47.768 --> 00:31:48.792
Over 30 armed guards

00:31:48.835 --> 00:31:50.666
are converging
on the storage facility.

00:31:50.704 --> 00:31:52.695
All available power
to the transporters.

00:31:52.739 --> 00:31:54.502
Let's try to get them
out of there.

00:31:54.541 --> 00:31:57.977
Even Theseus could not
negotiate this labyrinth.

00:31:58.011 --> 00:31:59.501
Not without a compass.

00:32:00.814 --> 00:32:02.714
Your compass is speaking to you.

00:32:04.051 --> 00:32:05.518
This way.

00:32:24.237 --> 00:32:26.501
A trove of invention.

00:32:30.777 --> 00:32:33.473
The prince has done
well for himself.

00:32:33.513 --> 00:32:36.346
Phasers...

00:32:36.383 --> 00:32:38.510
warp plasma injectors...

00:32:38.552 --> 00:32:40.383
a site-to-site transporter.

00:32:45.759 --> 00:32:47.454
Your computer?

00:32:47.494 --> 00:32:48.620
Yes.

00:32:52.065 --> 00:32:53.999
Computer, do you recognize
my voice?

00:32:54.101 --> 00:32:54.999
Affirmative.

00:32:55.102 --> 00:32:56.899
Well, that's a start.

00:32:56.937 --> 00:32:58.461
Che bella!

00:32:58.505 --> 00:33:00.439
There's a mechanical woman
inside.

00:33:00.474 --> 00:33:02.169
In a way, yes.

00:33:02.209 --> 00:33:04.939
Initiate a level-4
induction relay overload.

00:33:04.978 --> 00:33:07.139
That procedure
is not recommended.

00:33:07.180 --> 00:33:09.944
Command override:
Janeway-pi-one-one-zero.

00:33:09.983 --> 00:33:11.780
Authorization confirmed.

00:33:11.818 --> 00:33:13.342
Initiating overload.

00:33:16.390 --> 00:33:17.357
That's it.

00:33:17.391 --> 00:33:18.653
And now?

00:33:18.692 --> 00:33:21.092
We wait for the Portuguese.

00:33:21.128 --> 00:33:23.062
Commander, I'm detecting
a power surge

00:33:23.096 --> 00:33:24.688
in the subspace frequency range.

00:33:24.731 --> 00:33:26.096
It could be the processor.

00:33:26.133 --> 00:33:27.100
Lock on.

00:33:27.134 --> 00:33:29.295
Increase power
to the confinement beam.

00:33:29.336 --> 00:33:30.303
With any luck,

00:33:30.337 --> 00:33:31.565
we might be able
to pull the Captain

00:33:31.605 --> 00:33:32.663
out of there along with it.

00:33:39.913 --> 00:33:41.141
Step close, Leonardo.

00:33:41.181 --> 00:33:42.478
We're going for a ride.

00:33:42.516 --> 00:33:43.744
I don't understand.

00:33:44.785 --> 00:33:46.082
Trust me.

00:34:11.344 --> 00:34:13.335
The building is probably
surrounded by now.

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:14.608
There's only one way out.

00:34:18.351 --> 00:34:19.716
Maestro, come here.

00:34:19.753 --> 00:34:22.813
Catarina,
what just happened to me?

00:34:24.057 --> 00:34:25.888
I was shot... yet I live.

00:34:25.926 --> 00:34:28.292
Such things are not possible.

00:34:34.434 --> 00:34:37.631
This is an invention
from another land.

00:34:37.671 --> 00:34:40.333
It's called
a site-to-site transporter.

00:34:40.373 --> 00:34:41.704
In the blink of an eye,

00:34:41.742 --> 00:34:43.801
it can move us
out of this building

00:34:43.844 --> 00:34:45.971
and a few kilometers
away from here.

00:34:46.012 --> 00:34:47.343
How?

00:34:47.380 --> 00:34:49.405
Come on.

00:34:57.724 --> 00:34:59.658
I must have an explanation.

00:35:01.061 --> 00:35:03.723
Leonardo, you've always said

00:35:03.764 --> 00:35:07.200
that it's a poor apprentice
who can't surpass her master.

00:35:07.234 --> 00:35:10.101
There are things in this world

00:35:10.137 --> 00:35:13.334
that I understand,
and you don't.

00:35:20.680 --> 00:35:22.773
Madonna mia.

00:35:28.655 --> 00:35:30.179
The processor is on board.

00:35:30.223 --> 00:35:31.747
The Captain?

00:35:31.792 --> 00:35:33.419
Still on the planet.

00:35:33.460 --> 00:35:34.950
Commander.

00:35:37.330 --> 00:35:40.265
13 vessels are approaching
Voyager from the surface.

00:35:40.300 --> 00:35:42.200
Tom, take us
into a higher orbit.

00:35:42.235 --> 00:35:43.259
Bridge to Torres.

00:35:43.303 --> 00:35:45.601
I want that processor
back on line.

00:35:45.639 --> 00:35:47.129
We've still got
a Captain done there.

00:35:47.174 --> 00:35:48.163
Acknowledged.

00:35:56.917 --> 00:35:58.544
I cannot believe it.

00:35:58.585 --> 00:35:59.984
I will not believe it.

00:36:00.020 --> 00:36:04.013
My mind cannot accept
the evidence of my eyes.

00:36:04.057 --> 00:36:06.753
Is this sorcery?
Are we in purgatory?

00:36:06.793 --> 00:36:07.919
Neither.
You said yourself

00:36:07.994 --> 00:36:09.484
this place was full
of marvels.

00:36:09.529 --> 00:36:11.690
Marvels, yes,
but this is magic...

00:36:11.731 --> 00:36:13.494
enchantment, not science.

00:36:13.533 --> 00:36:16.730
And I refuse to believe
in enchantment.

00:36:16.770 --> 00:36:18.362
I'll explain later.
We've got to keep moving.

00:36:18.405 --> 00:36:19.497
No!

00:36:20.373 --> 00:36:23.308
I must understand.

00:36:23.343 --> 00:36:25.675
Catarina...

00:36:25.712 --> 00:36:28.180
to see objects disappear
into thin air...

00:36:28.214 --> 00:36:32.082
to see lightning
pass through my body...

00:36:34.621 --> 00:36:36.213
Are we spirits?

00:36:36.256 --> 00:36:39.316
Catarina... am I dead?

00:36:39.359 --> 00:36:41.259
Let me ask you something.

00:36:41.294 --> 00:36:44.525
If you were something
other than a human being...

00:36:44.564 --> 00:36:46.657
if you were a different
kind of animal...

00:36:48.001 --> 00:36:50.868
if you were a small bird,
a sparrow...

00:36:50.904 --> 00:36:52.531
what would your world be like?

00:36:53.773 --> 00:36:55.798
I should make my home
in a tree

00:36:55.842 --> 00:36:57.503
in the branch of an elm.

00:36:57.544 --> 00:37:02.607
I should hunt insects for food,
straw for my nest

00:37:02.649 --> 00:37:05.482
and in the springtime,
I should sing for a companion.

00:37:05.518 --> 00:37:08.043
Then you would know nothing
of the politics of Florence?

00:37:08.088 --> 00:37:10.318
The cutting of marble,
or mathematics?

00:37:10.357 --> 00:37:11.324
Of course not.

00:37:11.358 --> 00:37:12.325
But why not?

00:37:12.359 --> 00:37:14.020
My mind would be too small.

00:37:15.362 --> 00:37:18.058
As a sparrow, your mind
would be too small

00:37:18.098 --> 00:37:20.157
even with the best of teachers?

00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:23.328
If Aristotle himself
were to perch on my branch

00:37:23.370 --> 00:37:26.897
and lecture till he fell off
from exhaustion...

00:37:26.940 --> 00:37:30.034
still the limits of my mind

00:37:30.076 --> 00:37:32.442
would prevent me
from understanding.

00:37:32.479 --> 00:37:34.879
And as a man, can you accept

00:37:34.914 --> 00:37:37.144
that there may be
certain realities

00:37:37.183 --> 00:37:40.414
beyond the limits
of your comprehension?

00:37:43.256 --> 00:37:45.315
If I could not accept that...

00:37:47.861 --> 00:37:50.091
then I would be a fool.

00:37:50.130 --> 00:37:51.324
Spread out! You...

00:37:51.364 --> 00:37:52.353
Come on.

00:37:54.434 --> 00:37:57.369
Catarina, this way,
up the hill.

00:37:57.404 --> 00:37:59.099
I know just the escape.

00:38:02.876 --> 00:38:05.709
Torres to Bridge.
We're in business.

00:38:05.745 --> 00:38:10.045
We've got full navigation...
full propulsion

00:38:10.083 --> 00:38:11.243
and full transporters.

00:38:11.284 --> 00:38:12.911
Good work B'Elanna.

00:38:12.986 --> 00:38:14.385
Sensors show the
Captain and da Vinci

00:38:14.421 --> 00:38:15.547
have left the structure.

00:38:15.588 --> 00:38:16.919
If we could dip
into a lower orbit,

00:38:16.990 --> 00:38:18.787
I should be able to lock on
to the mobile emitter.

00:38:18.825 --> 00:38:20.315
Set the confinement beam wide

00:38:20.360 --> 00:38:23.261
and prepare to transport
both of them back to the ship.

00:38:23.296 --> 00:38:25.423
How close do we have to be?

00:38:25.465 --> 00:38:27.456
At least 500 kilometers
from the surface.

00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:29.798
Those ships will try
to block our descent.

00:38:29.836 --> 00:38:32.236
Ready for some fancy flying?

00:38:32.272 --> 00:38:33.762
You bet.

00:38:40.380 --> 00:38:42.541
Momento, Catarina.

00:38:46.286 --> 00:38:49.449
Escape, signorina, is very near.

00:38:49.489 --> 00:38:51.389
I'm starting to wonder.

00:38:51.424 --> 00:38:53.255
Where are you, Chakotay?

00:38:54.461 --> 00:38:55.689
Help me to the summit.

00:39:10.343 --> 00:39:12.504
We're at 1,000 kilometers.

00:39:12.545 --> 00:39:14.911
950...

00:39:15.014 --> 00:39:16.777
900.

00:39:16.816 --> 00:39:20.547
The ships are powering weapons.

00:39:20.587 --> 00:39:22.521
Go to Red Alert.

00:39:28.428 --> 00:39:30.020
Shields are holding.

00:39:30.063 --> 00:39:31.894
850 kilometers.

00:39:33.967 --> 00:39:35.867
Evasive maneuvers.

00:39:35.902 --> 00:39:38.530
When Petrarch climbed
Mount Verdoun

00:39:38.571 --> 00:39:40.766
and saw all Europe below him,

00:39:40.807 --> 00:39:44.106
he knew he was witnessing
the birth of a new age.

00:39:44.144 --> 00:39:46.738
He was witnessing
the Renaissance...

00:39:46.780 --> 00:39:48.509
the rebirth of our world.

00:39:48.548 --> 00:39:50.948
So, Catarina,
at this summit here,

00:39:51.050 --> 00:39:53.280
you and I will be reborn.

00:39:53.319 --> 00:39:57.688
Reborn... with wings.

00:40:16.876 --> 00:40:19.367
This could be a problem.

00:40:19.412 --> 00:40:21.403
Hurry, there's not much time.

00:40:23.449 --> 00:40:26.612
Sir, they seem to be
on the edge of precipice,

00:40:26.653 --> 00:40:28.814
but we're still
too high for transport.

00:40:29.823 --> 00:40:31.882
You've made some improvements.

00:40:31.925 --> 00:40:34.553
I took your advice
after the last attempt

00:40:34.594 --> 00:40:36.687
and increased
the reach of the wings.

00:40:36.729 --> 00:40:38.390
And the angle of attack?

00:40:38.431 --> 00:40:39.398
Yes, yes, that, too.

00:40:39.432 --> 00:40:42.196
Unfortunately, the River
Arno is quite absent.

00:40:42.235 --> 00:40:43.964
This time, if we fail,

00:40:44.003 --> 00:40:46.437
only the stones
will break our fall.

00:40:46.472 --> 00:40:48.770
The wing is stationary,
that's good.

00:40:48.808 --> 00:40:50.275
This looks like duranium alloy.

00:40:50.310 --> 00:40:51.572
It should be light enough.

00:40:51.611 --> 00:40:54.375
Catarina,
this time it will work.

00:40:57.250 --> 00:40:58.808
Let's find out.

00:40:59.819 --> 00:41:01.582
I'm reading weapons fire
on the surface

00:41:01.621 --> 00:41:02.918
near the Captain's position.

00:41:02.956 --> 00:41:04.947
We're running out
of time, sir.

00:41:05.024 --> 00:41:06.616
700 kilometers.

00:41:06.659 --> 00:41:09.127
Hold on, Kathryn,
just a few more seconds.

00:41:09.162 --> 00:41:10.959
- Together... up.
- Andiamo.

00:41:25.645 --> 00:41:27.340
Catarina, we're flying!

00:41:27.380 --> 00:41:29.473
- Like the birds!
- Like the birds!

00:41:47.967 --> 00:41:49.935
I have a fix on the Captain.

00:41:49.969 --> 00:41:52.267
They are... in mid-air

00:41:52.305 --> 00:41:55.365
on what appears to be
a crude gliding apparatus.

00:41:55.408 --> 00:41:56.272
500 kilometers!

00:41:56.309 --> 00:41:57.276
I'm locking on.

00:41:57.310 --> 00:41:59.107
Broad confinement beam.

00:41:59.145 --> 00:42:00.510
Energize.

00:42:09.255 --> 00:42:10.654
Got them!

00:42:10.690 --> 00:42:13.386
I beamed the whole contraption
into Cargo Bay 1.

00:42:13.426 --> 00:42:15.155
Get us out of here, Mr. Paris.

00:42:18.531 --> 00:42:22.490
Captain's Log, Stardate 51408.3.

00:42:22.535 --> 00:42:24.799
We're back on course
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:42:24.837 --> 00:42:26.828
With the ship's computer
and the Doctor's emitter

00:42:26.872 --> 00:42:28.339
returned to proper places,

00:42:28.374 --> 00:42:31.070
I've set aside some time
to check on the Maestro.

00:42:40.586 --> 00:42:42.816
Leonardo, where are you going?

00:42:42.855 --> 00:42:44.152
France.

00:42:44.190 --> 00:42:47.125
These Florentines
do not deserve my genius.

00:42:47.159 --> 00:42:48.990
I have written
to the king of France,

00:42:49.095 --> 00:42:51.461
telling him of my adventures
in the New World

00:42:51.497 --> 00:42:55.729
and invited him to soar with me
off the towers of his castle.

00:42:55.768 --> 00:42:58.134
Are you sure that's a good idea?

00:42:58.170 --> 00:42:59.637
Why not?

00:42:59.672 --> 00:43:01.765
We ourselves have tested
the design.

00:43:01.807 --> 00:43:04.241
But the materials...

00:43:04.277 --> 00:43:07.246
you'll never find
those metals in France.

00:43:07.280 --> 00:43:10.340
No?
Then others will suffice.

00:43:10.383 --> 00:43:12.943
Machines that fly
through the air!

00:43:13.052 --> 00:43:15.213
Lightning flung
from one's hands!

00:43:15.254 --> 00:43:19.520
Mechanical women
who live in boxes!

00:43:19.558 --> 00:43:21.958
These things I have seen!

00:43:21.994 --> 00:43:24.588
And these things
I must recreate.

00:43:24.630 --> 00:43:26.063
And who knows?

00:43:26.098 --> 00:43:28.123
Possibly improve upon.

00:43:28.167 --> 00:43:31.364
Leonardo, I think
that little flight of ours

00:43:31.404 --> 00:43:32.735
went to your head.

00:43:32.772 --> 00:43:35.263
And my heart.

00:43:35.308 --> 00:43:37.742
My oldest memory, Catarina,

00:43:37.777 --> 00:43:41.406
is of a great bird
perched on my bed,

00:43:41.447 --> 00:43:45.315
its feathers open towards me
as if summoning me.

00:43:45.351 --> 00:43:50.084
Now, you yourself
have accused me of giving up,

00:43:50.122 --> 00:43:53.353
of, uh, failing
to complete my project.

00:43:53.392 --> 00:43:54.381
I was trying to encourage...

00:43:54.427 --> 00:43:55.394
No, no.

00:43:55.428 --> 00:43:56.452
You were right.

00:43:56.495 --> 00:44:01.125
All my life
I have wanted to fly.

00:44:01.167 --> 00:44:04.068
Perhaps my failure to do so

00:44:04.103 --> 00:44:08.836
has caused my heart
to remain in flight.

00:44:08.874 --> 00:44:12.275
Leaping from one thing
to another.

00:44:12.311 --> 00:44:14.142
Never satisfied.

00:44:15.715 --> 00:44:17.774
Never complete.

00:44:17.817 --> 00:44:20.752
And now that you've
actually flown?

00:44:22.755 --> 00:44:26.521
Now, who knows
what I cannot accomplish.

00:44:27.693 --> 00:44:30.287
I'd like to find out.

00:44:31.297 --> 00:44:34.164
Give my regards
to the king of France.

00:44:48.547 --> 00:44:50.947
Catarina,

00:44:50.983 --> 00:44:53.611
will you walk with me
to my carriage?

00:44:53.652 --> 00:44:55.176
It would be my pleasure.
